{"t": 1795089396.8675249, "tool": "analyze", "code": "def fitpoly(ie,jt):\n    cols=[];names=[]\n    for i in range(ie+1):\n        for j in range(jt+1):\n            cols.append(eps**i*T**j); names.append((i,j))\n    A=np.array(cols).T\n    c,*_=np.linalg.lstsq(A,sigma,rcond=None)\n    r=sigma-A@c\n    return np.mean(r**2)/np.var(sigma), names, c\nfor ie in [2,3,4,5]:\n    for jt in [1,2,3,4]:\n        v,_,_=fitpoly(ie,jt)\n        print(ie,jt,v)\n", "out": "2 1 0.007828534715789566\n2 2 5.839923946065055e-24\n2 3 5.5662732771004664e-24\n2 4 5.533290508272423e-24\n3 1 0.007790262330101044\n3 2 5.650286812211359e-24\n3 3 5.414145631640334e-24\n3 4 5.385710994353774e-24\n4 1 0.0076956829308528095\n4 2 5.644650709503727e-24\n4 3 5.40359654097784e-24\n4 4 5.34496867761497e-24\n5 1 0.007692723318716624\n5 2 5.5605445418295395e-24\n5 3 5.32688806522838e-24\n5 4 2.790269521672582e-23\n"}
